Hi again!

Just learned once more how nasty R can be: One can change the calling enviroment of a function, such that this code snippet

    if("init" %in% names(stan_args)) {
        if(is.function(stan_args$init))
            environment(stan_args$init) <- list2env(stan_data)
    }
    fit <- do.call(stan_run, stan_args)
Does what I want, i.e. if init is a function, then I make the data the encapuslating environment for init. Maybe this could become the default for rstan?

Best,
Sebastian

