Bill,

What do you mean by system('make -v') fails?  I think the problem is that you cannot R cannot use `gnu make` so it cannot install Rcpp from source because it will use make as installing rstan would need.  Besides, if make is found, one needs to make sure it is the one that is packaged in rtools.  For example, one would expect the following:

> system('where make')
c:\Rtools\bin\make.exe

Jiqiang

