Interesting... actually "y_raw ~ normal(0,1)" is the true embodiment
of your sentence just above, and the prior for "y" should really take
the distribution for order statistics drawn from the normal, surely.
Sorting doesn't affect the marginal distributions of "y" but it does
affect their joint distribution; so it seems to me that both models
above, since they specify independent normal distributions for the
sorted values, imply a dependence structure for the unsorted values
which may in many cases be unintended?

