>>> So this makes sense if we're thinking of the ordered vector
>>> as the result of K independent draws that are sorted.
>>
>> Interesting... actually "y_raw ~ normal(0,1)" is the true embodiment
>> of your sentence just above, and the prior for "y" should really take
>> the distribution for order statistics drawn from the normal, surely.
>
> It does that implicitly by sorting. If you set
>
>   y <- sort(y_raw);
