Dear Stan list,

>> for(k in 1:(N_type - 1))
>>    pi[k] <- exp(gamma_type[k] + delta[k] * x[n]);
>> pi[N_type] <- 0;

I've been looking how they resolve this in mnrfit in matlab (which I'm familiar with):
http://www.mathworks.ch/ch/help/stats/multinomial-models-for-nominal-responses.html
When I'm not totally wrong that would

pi[N_type] <- 1 - sum(pi[1:(N_type-1)]);

Or maybe we could use the softmax where when we set gamma_type[k] + delta[k] * x[n]  == (equvialent for all) 1
for k = N_type?

Andre

