> It's discussed in the manual and http://arxiv.org/abs/1312.0906, and is displayed in the bin/print output.

For RStan users, it is a bit harder but can be displayed with get_sampler_params(), as in:

dogs <- stan_demo("dogs")
sampler_params <- get_sampler_params(dogs)
names(sampler_params) <- colnames(dogs)
lapply(sampler_params, FUN = function(x) table(x[,"n_divergent__"]))
$`chain:1`

   0    1
1991    9

$`chain:2`

   0    1
1991    9

$`chain:3`

   0    1
1991    9

$`chain:4`

   0    1
1993    7

> lapply(sampler_params, FUN = function(x) which(x[,"n_divergent__"] > 0))
$`chain:1`
[1]   2   3   4  10  48 251 252 452 952

$`chain:2`
[1]   2   3   4 102 252 452 518 952 987

$`chain:3`
[1]   2   3   4 102 152 252 452 532 952

$`chain:4`
[1]   2   3 102 152 251 252 952

Not too bad. Appears to be more likely to diverge after a window switch.

Ben

