Hi,

I've trouble concerning the possibility to compute a Bayesian p_value in the Rstan code.
in a previous thread (Simple latent Poisson time series model: Sampling versus Optimizing), i saw this code:

yrep[i] ~ Poisson(lambda[i]);

and then computing the p_value as:

b.pvalue ~ (yrep[i] > y[i]) -0.5 *   (yrep[i] == y[i]);

which seems particularly easy... but I don't understand where y[i] come from.

If I use the following model:

y[i] ~ Normal(mu[i],sigma);

I have no idea how to compute a yrep[i] . I saw how to assess a p-value after simulation, but I would like to do it direclty in the code.

Could someone give an example on how to compute a Bayesian p-value with a simple linear gaussian regression ?

Thank you

