Hi, David.  Did you happen to try Stan with the unconstrained parameterization but implementing the constraint implicitly using Ben’s idea:

parameters {
  vector[K] sqrt_beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[K] beta;
  for(k in 1:K) beta[k] <- square(sqrt_beta[k]);
}

Or using the unconstrained parameterization but implementing the constraint using the step function as recommended by Marcus, I think?  (In that case you just have to make sure you use positive values for the inits)?

Andrew

