> > Hi, David.  Did you happen to try Stan with the unconstrained parameterization but implementing the constraint implicitly using Ben’s idea:
>
> Oh, I forgot to try this idea. It indeed makes the solution more stable. However, comes with 2 problems:
> When it works, it's very slow (about 3 seconds.)
> Every few tries it  doe snot work, giving this error: Optimization terminated with error: Line search failed to achieve a sufficient decrease, no more progress can be made.
