> https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/stan-users/HBewhdW1u88

Trans-dimensional models are a different problem altogether, and I don't know of any algorithm that works particularly well outside of knowing a reasonable truncation point a priori and building a model of constant dimension.  Then again, we haven't spent a tremendous amount of time trying to build and fit these models.

Interestingly enough there are some possible generalizations to algorithms like HMC to these models, but the math is really complicated and somewhat obscure, so they won't be coming any time soon.

