L-BFGS-B is implemented in R if that helps.

Steve Johnson of NLOPT has implemented box constraints in almost all of his algorithms using a method based on Box (1965) {and isn't that apropos :) }. See <http://ab-initio.mit.edu/wiki/index.php/NLopt_Algorithms#Nelder-Mead_Simplex> where he summarizes it by saying any time a point is returned outside the bound constraint, what is returned is the (closest, I guess) constraint itself. That may be simple to implement as a wrapper to any general optimization algorithm.

Avi

