> * removing ‘/usr/local/sage-6.3beta6/local/lib/R/library/rstan’
>
> The downloaded source packages are in
>     ‘/tmp/Rtmp0xOKsZ/downloaded_packages’
> Erreur dans library(rstan) : there is no package called ‘rstan’
> De plus : Message d'avis :
> In install.packages("rstan", type = "source") :
>   installation of package ‘rstan’ had non-zero exit status
>
> Any hint ? I note that rstan seems to need its very own versin of Rcpp and RcppEigen. Could this be the cause of the problems ?

They are unmodified Rcpp and RcppEigen from CRAN. My guess is that there is something going on with Sage that causes it to not link correctly. I'll try to figure it out. Can you install rstan outside of R via Sage? And you are using the g++ that comes with Sage or the system one (and if so what version)?

Ben

