Same difference...

>
> Can you get the latest version of Rcpp to install
> and run a simple example?  (Is the simple example still
> in our install instructions?)

I ran "update.packages(ask=FALSE, checkBuilt=TRUE)" just before trying to install Sage 2.4.0.

The Rcpp update was uneventful. *After* my failed install_rstan() attempt, the same update attempt yelded nothing to update.

[ BTW : I wonder about the necessity for the install_rstan script to install an already installed.package, if the latest available package on CRAN is sufficent... ]

> I don't know what you mean by "very own version of Rcpp".
> Is RStan somehow unusual in how it depends on other R
> packages?

That's what your install script seems to believe. Why not make it depend on sufficienciently recent version of CRAN packages instead ?

