I think I have been advocating getting rstan onto CRAN for more than two years

https://groups.google.com/d/msg/stan-dev/wIpu_otqK10/H5OZnHOX5PQJ

and am the only Stan developer that is strongly in favor of getting rstan onto CRAN, so you are shouting at the wrong person. BH 1.54.0-x was the first version of the BH package that would build rstan and rstan 1.0.1 was rejected from CRAN on September 15, 2012 largely for bundling the necessary parts of Boost. Since then, we have dealt with one installation problem after another on Windows and Mac OSX (and occasionally Linux) that has culminated in the script you are keen to get rid of, which has reduced installation problems of rstan 2.3.0 and rstan 2.4.0 to a trickle. For rstan 2.4.0, we switched to depend on the R packages BH and RcppEigen instead of bundling Boost and Eigen to see if there were any problems, so that we could try again to get rstan onto CRAN for the next rstan version. That seems to be going fine and rstan 2.4.0 builds on the CRAN server (because the CRAN server uses the default CXXFLAGS), but there are a few more things we would have to do to make rstan fully CRAN-compliant.

Ben

