Because I don't know how to obtain the T-dimensional vector( or row-vector) from the array of 2-dimensional positive ordered.
Off course I don't wanna use for-loop, as much as possible.For example , the original is
===

  # linear predictor
  Yp <- bl + a1 .* X1 + a2 .* X2;

===
It, elementwise production,  makes me release from for-loop ,and I love it.
But it seems that a[,1] or a[,2] are inefficient way to write in stan.

How can I pick T-dimensional vector up from orderd[2] a[T] ?
I can't find the way to do that in manual. sorry.

