Ignore my suggestion about the bivariate modeling. If alpha and gamma represent between and within lot variation, you certainly don't want to tangle them up. Bivariate modeling of alpha and gamma would make the model less identifiable, as fordifferent values of the rho parameter, you can arrive at exactly the same posterior density (given a uniform prior on rho) by rescaling the alpha and gamma parameters. So I guess that only leaves my question about what the plots represent!

